2026-11-12T01:26:02.6195670Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-12T01:26:02.6246710Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-12T01:26:02.6247550Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-12T01:26:02.6263660Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-12T01:26:02.6264960Z 
2026-11-12T01:26:02.6265880Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-12T01:26:02.6267550Z 
2026-11-12T01:26:02.6267960Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-12T01:26:02.6268890Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-12T01:26:02.6269220Z 
2026-11-12T01:26:02.6269430Z If you would like to
2026-11-12T01:26:02.6269740Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-12T01:26:02.6270170Z 
2026-11-12T01:26:02.6270870Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-12T01:26:02.6271190Z   $ sh ./install-nix
